-- ============================================================================
-- Bug #263: mappings over a MESSAGE DEFINITION could not be authored
-- ============================================================================
--
-- Symptom (before fix):
--   MDL had `with json structure` and `with xml schema` and no third form, so a
--   mapping sourced from a message definition — 74 of the 327 mapping documents
--   in the demo apps, the second-largest gap after the array root — could not be
--   written at all. Worse, DESCRIBE dropped the source clause entirely AND its
--   output parsed, so `describe` -> `exec` rebuilt the mapping bound to nothing.
--   70 of the 74 were in that silent-loss class (#260).
--
-- What a message definition is, and why it needed its own builder:
--   It is not a payload sample. It is derived from the DOMAIN MODEL — every node
--   names an entity or an attribute — and it carries two names per node: its own
--   ("Emails") and the singular one its items take ("Email"). A mapping over it
--   stores BOTH path families:
--
--     value  attr=AgentCore.Email.From  json=(Array)|(Object)|From  xml=Emails|Email|From
--
--   unbounded node   xml += ExposedName|ExposedItemName   json += ExposedName|(Object)
--   single node      xml += ExposedName                   json += ExposedName
--   root, unbounded  xml  = ExposedName|ExposedItemName   json  = (Array)|(Object)
--
--   Measured on AgentCore.MesDef_Email, AgentCore.MesDef_WorkflowDetails and
--   Email_Connector.MD_EmailTemplate (EnquiriesManagement demo app, 11.13).
--
-- Not a "map everything" shorthand:
--   Of the ten message-definition mappings in the demo apps, six map every
--   exposed node and four map a strict subset (58 of 96, 27 of 30, 28 of 30,
--   26 of 27) — so the body is load-bearing, not redundant.
--
-- Validation:
--   Authoring AgentCore.MesDef_Email.Email from MDL reproduces Studio Pro's own
--   AgentCore.Email_Import element for element — entity, handling, backup,
--   exposed names, occurrences, both path families and the value data types.
--   mxbuild 11.13 reports no new errors.
--
-- This script needs a project that HAS the definition; message definitions are
-- not authorable from MDL (they are read-only here) and this file is a syntax
-- reference. The executable coverage is
-- mdl/executor/mapping_messagedefinition_test.go, which runs against the real
-- definitions in mdl/executor/testdata/mapping-fixtures/.
-- ============================================================================

-- The reference is THREE parts: the definitions live inside a collection
-- document, so it is Module.Collection.Definition.
create or modify import mapping AgentCore.IMM_Email
  folder 'Mappings'
  with message definition AgentCore.MesDef_Email.Email
{
  create AgentCore.Email {
    From = From,
    Content = Content,
    Subject = Subject
  }
};

-- Export twin. The root object handling is Parameter, Find below it, exactly as
-- for a JSON-structure export mapping.
create or modify export mapping AgentCore.EXM_Email
  folder 'Mappings'
  with message definition AgentCore.MesDef_Email.Email
{
  AgentCore.Email {
    From = From,
    Content = Content,
    Subject = Subject
  }
};
